  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Guests can leave a short comment at the lending station or at a return point.\", \"decision\": \"How should guests offer feedback about the cup loan?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe lending station asks guests what would make return easier and forwards comments to the return points. Feedback can improve the process before those loans end.\nBoth lending and return stations collect comments on a shared sheet that volunteers review between service blocks. Feedback from the beginning and end of loans is considered together.\nVolunteers invite a comment at return and send it to the lending station with the next crate update. Feedback comes from guests who have completed the loan."
    }
  ],
